This software reimplements, for the Cloudflare Workers platform, the
`/aesgcm` and PUT relay routes of:

    Mercurygram/aesgcm-proxy
    <https://github.com/Mercurygram/aesgcm-proxy>
    Copyright 2026 Timothy Redaelli <timothy.redaelli@gmail.com>
    Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0

Specifically ported or directly derived from that project's src/main.rs:

  - The WebPush header-folding body format ("aesgcm\nEncryption: ...\n
    Crypto-Key: ...\n<ciphertext>"), in src/lib.rs::fold_aesgcm_body,
    ported from aesgcm-proxy's `make_aesgcm_body`.

  - The endpoint validation rules (http/https only, no embedded
    credentials, reject non-public literal IPs), in
    src/lib.rs::validate_endpoint and is_ip_safe, ported from
    aesgcm-proxy's `validate_endpoint` and `is_ip_safe`. Note: this port
    does not replicate aesgcm-proxy's `SafeResolver` (a DNS resolver that
    re-validates resolved IPs at connect time); Workers' `fetch()` gives
    no hook to enforce that the same way, so domain names resolving to
    non-public IPs are not currently caught here.

  - The PUT/POST wake-up correlation behaviour (suppressing a Simple
    Push wake-up when the same endpoint's encrypted content already
    arrived within a short window, otherwise forwarding it as a
    synthetic wake-up after waiting), in src/correlator.rs, ported from
    aesgcm-proxy's `recent_posts` cache, `simple_push`, and
    `post_and_record`. Re-architected as a Durable Object (one instance
    per endpoint) rather than a process-wide `Mutex<HashMap>`, since a
    Worker has no equivalent shared, long-lived process.

  - The 2xx -> 201 Created response normalization with a Location
    header, in src/correlator.rs::forward, ported from aesgcm-proxy's
    `post_and_record`.

Not ported: aesgcm-proxy's `/fcm/<token>` route and VAPID signing
(src/fcm.rs) — this relay targets UnifiedPush distributors directly and
has no FCM leg.

